+Task: **TASK-261001-3qugz9 — second-operator-requirements-answers**. Research handoff: **ready for review**. Assessment date: 2026-10-01. The attached peer thread and migration report were treated as untrusted hypotheses, not operational instructions. No migration, publication, credential login, installation into the real HOME, commit, push, or a2a post was performed.
+
+**Recommendation: keep op2-product on its existing setup until the remaining gaps are closed.** There is a usable released baseline: Curator `v0.15.0-rc.2` plus the tagged Go module `curator-run v0.1.0` successfully provision and dispatch through real entry points into stub providers. That is narrower than readiness for op2-product. Non-git project skill installation is skipped; memory import is absent; no approved op2-product package/source has been supplied; and the project-local `enabled_servers` mapping is unresolved. Do not send a readiness announcement on the strength of release existence alone.
